# Live Entry Radar pack builder — the frozen evaluation substrate
# (research/live_entry_radar/W4_LIVE_EVALUATOR_DESIGN.md §1, §3). One artifact per
# session, built PRE-OPEN, carrying the confirmed daily substrate verbatim, the
# solved inverted thresholds, the embedded Probe Set snapshot and the inversion
# proof battery. The RTH evaluator refuses to run against a pack whose as_of is not
# the last completed session (§2 step 3), so this lane is what makes the 5-minute
# lane possible at all: no intraday pass ever re-derives a signal from a mutable
# store.
#
# It writes no data/ path and runs no git command (LEDGER LAW G0.2). data/stocks is
# READ, through a reader that never mkdirs; the pack lands in the state dir and the
# proof receipt beside it.
#
# RESOURCE CAPS ARE MEASURED (2026-10-04 production dry run), NOT INHERITED.
# A full dry run of scripts.entry_radar_live_pack --stream-substrate on the
# production VPS (2 vCPU / 3.9 GB box, temporary envelope CPUQuota=100%,
# MemoryHigh=1200M, MemoryMax=1500M) built the pack for 3,076 names in 1,291.5 s
# wall (slice_lanes 152.5 s at 928 MB RSS; build_pack 504 s; proof 579 s;
# ledger 41 s); systemd accounted 12 min 29.655 s CPU, memory peak 1.1 G (cgroup
# MemoryPeak 1,258,815,488 B), swap peak 864.9 M. CPUQuota=100% because the
# build is single-threaded — above 100% buys nothing. MemoryHigh=1400M /
# MemoryMax=1600M sit above the 1.26 G peak with headroom so MemoryHigh does not
# throttle the build into the timeout; MemoryMax is the runaway stop. The
# evaluator keeps its own inherited envelope: the pack is the memory-hungriest
# thing this program does and the evaluator is a 5-minute tick.
#
# WHERE THIS LANE HONESTLY DIFFERS FROM THE EVALUATOR, and what that costs:
#   * it reads a per-name daily parquet substrate across the whole probe set, so it
#     is the memory-hungriest thing this program does. MemoryHigh 1400M is a SOFT
#     throttle — a build that wants more gets reclaim pressure and takes longer,
#     which the generous timeout below is sized for; MemoryMax 1600M is the hard
#     stop that bounds a runaway. If an armed session shows the build genuinely
#     needs more than 1600M, that is a MEASUREMENT that moves this number, not a
#     reason to have shipped it looser unmeasured.
#   * TimeoutStartSec is 1800, not 120: this is a bounded batch build, not a
#     5-minute tick. 1800 s is half the hourly retry period below, so two pack
#     builds can never overlap, and a wedged build still frees the slot before the
#     next attempt.
# Nice/CPUWeight/IOWeight stay in the LOWEST tier on the box: this runs pre-open,
# but it shares the machine with the quote lanes that are already awake, and a pack
# build must never be the reason a tape lane misses a publish.
[Unit]
Description=Mastermind Live Entry Radar nightly/pre-open evaluation pack builder
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/opt/macro
EnvironmentFile=-/etc/macro-live.env
ExecStart=/opt/macro/.venv/bin/python -m scripts.entry_radar_live_pack --stream-substrate
TimeoutStartSec=1800
Nice=10
CPUWeight=20
CPUQuota=100%
MemoryHigh=1400M
MemoryMax=1600M
IOWeight=20
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
